# Credentials and secrets.
#
# This repository is heading towards commercial use and will carry financial
# data. Nothing matching these patterns belongs in it. The exceptions at the
# end are deliberate: a throwaway TLS pair the packaging gate needs and the
# public ISRG root certificates the trust store ships. Both are documented in
# tests/fixtures/README.md, and the private key there is public by definition.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
.env
.env.*
.netrc
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*_rsa
*_ecdsa
*_ed25519
secrets.*
credentials.*
service-account*.json
!tests/fixtures/xapt-tls-key.pem
!tests/fixtures/xapt-tls-cert.pem
!userspace/apps/trust/*.pem

# Release images are not committed. GitHub refuses any file over 100 MB, and a
# 227 MB ISO in history would be carried by every clone of this repository
# forever. The release note beside them is tracked; the image itself is
# published as a GitHub release asset and rebuilt from a tagged commit with
# make unified-image. Its SHA-256 is recorded in the note, so a downloaded
# image can be checked against what was gated.
release/*.iso
# The zip is tracked. It is about a tenth the size of the image, which puts it
# under GitHub's 100 MB limit, so the release can travel with the repository.
!release/*.iso.zip
